# Target C Level I run — live synthesis

Date: 2026-10-04. Branch: `research/sol/target-c-level1-gpt61-2026-10-04`.
Starting main: `f539af073a691c13327a0a7fef3c746fb7704e5f`.
Starting state: `2026-09-14.audit.51`. Imported main `0351e2c529e01750f7aceb87f8f6f0cb9c21dea7`, state `2026-10-05.audit.54`. Level I open; C-I closed; C-II open.

Lifecycle refresh: the October structural and return/reciprocal promotion
audits now make the hull-depletion floor, augmented rank, positive residual,
contact regularity, reciprocal internal-train graph, outer-train determination,
global face quotas, joint separator capacity, terminal physical frustration
and loaded flat pentagon depletion canonical at their exact audited scopes.
Audit.54 also promotes the wall-disjoint pentagon bulk and embedded-wall
shielding/refill theorem at their exact audited scopes and registers the
fixed-wall regressions. Later one-pin and two-side polynomial refill,
two-pin capacity, multishear traffic, and universal pentagon-capacity
claims remain unreviewed. Older
paragraphs below record discovery-time classifications; this refresh and
the state lock control their current authority.

## Trusted input and exact frontier

Canonical: core-scoped ZR/ZF; positive unloaded equilibrium; harmonic trapping
and disjoint attachment cells; Type-II disk/rhombus saturation; actual loaded
unit contacts are hull sides; Sections 120--123 signed return/global payment.
Contact-isolated points stay in the full source.

Personally checked proof-only input: #699's finite hull-occurrence/end count,
phase-depletion order of limits, remaining-train Mantel step and finite
synthesis. Base of #699: `596445ac32ffd45e2cbb8df9dbeba15be3465cf5` (the #696
multishear salvage squash). Squash of #699 is the starting main SHA; original
PR tip is `e54dc5be6f88516570c82af38ed7707deb22ac89`.

Put (s=\sqrt{\pi/(2\sqrt3)}). The live, now independently promoted hull-depletion inequality is

\[
5m_B+4S+2\sigma_R\ge2(\pi+s)D+5k+2(Q-f)+2(b-P_F)-o(D).
\]

Any further train subfamily carrying (o(D^2)) incident rhombi adds five
times its cardinality to the right. The scalar hull floor is
\(\mu_D\ge(\pi+s)/2+\varepsilon_*\) eventually, for a nonexplicit positive
gap. Terminal (q/D\to\pi) implies \(\liminf t_D\ge(3\pi+2s)/5\).
The old terminal windows near 1.95--1.96 and the terminal 1.860 collar scope
are empty. The disk perimeter limit alone is not terminality.

## New result in this run

[Global face quotas](../docs/reports/target_c_global_exceptional_face_return_quotas_2026-10-04.md):
for a minimum actual-contact separator from selected augmented-face boundaries
to actual loaded vertices,

\[
 Q_{\mathcal F}\le2|S|-2c_U-4c_K\le2|S|-4.
\]

The resulting globally vertex-disjoint unloaded-start returns satisfy a
simultaneous quota
\(r_f=\max(0,\lfloor(m_f-4)/2\rfloor-\ell_f)\) for every selected face.
This handles cross-face reuse and mesoscopic degree tails at the level of
face-indexed return count. It does not charge return length as face currency.
Classification: proved candidate awaiting independent audit and promotion.

[Joint bulk/defect capacity and spatial exclusion](../docs/reports/target_c_joint_bulk_defect_separator_capacity_2026-10-05.md):
for physical face and unloaded-rhombus demands behind one actual-contact
separator,

\[
2\sqrt{\pi(\sqrt3/2)(R-5k_I)_+}+Q_{\mathcal F}\le4|S|-4.
\]

In Type II this gives a joint endpoint bank of
(\pi D/4+Q_{\mathcal F}/4-o(D)), with a simultaneous quarter-defect face
quota and a \(\pi D/4-o(D)\) bulk quota. Uniform spatial exclusion:
(Q_{\mathcal F}\le(32+4\pi)r+18) when all selected boundaries lie in a
radius-(r) disk. A linear defect tail cannot be confined to one (o(D))
cluster, or to (o(D)) clusters whose radii sum to (o(D)). Classification:
proved candidates awaiting independent audit; no train-depletion charge yet.

[Outer-pocket Groemer phase depletion](../docs/reports/target_c_outer_pocket_groemer_phase_depletion_2026-10-05.md):
on the conditional branch (R_F=o(D)) with uniformly integrable outer-pocket
occurrence lengths, **every outer-ended train** carries only subquadratic
rhombus incidence. The surviving internal-to-internal train bank satisfies

\[
T_{\rm int}\ge(2s-o(1))D,\qquad
P_{\rm exc}\ge(4s-o(1))D+T_{\rm mix}.
\]

This excludes smaller internal banks/perimeters in that exact branch. It
also adds (5z_O) to (S), where (z_O=|\mathcal O_D|-|G_D|) and

\[
z_O\ge\max\{0,(3m_B+u_B-q)/2+d_D\}.
\]

This is an actual second-depletion theorem, conditional on small residual
and the outer-pocket tail condition. Neither condition is established for
all survivors. It creates no contacts and no source motion. Classification:
conditional theorem candidate awaiting independent audit.

For every fixed (K), the same deletion includes all degree-at-most-(K)
exceptional faces touching any actual unit loaded-hull side. With their
perimeter (P_{B,K}), the stronger charge is

\[
z_K\ge\max\{0,(3m_B+u_B-q+P_{B,K})/2+d_D\}.
\]

All quadratic bulk must remain on trains with **two unselected-face ends**;
their recipient face perimeter is at least (4sD-o(D)), plus the mixed
terminal count. This condition excludes the branch where all exceptional
faces have bounded degree and touch unit hull sides, subject to the stated
residual and outer-pocket tail hypotheses.

[Outer-train determination and marked-face bank synthesis](../docs/reports/target_c_outer_train_rank_groemer_bank_synthesis_2026-10-05.md):
the finite source-specific rank theorem gives

\[
|\mathcal O|\ge q-k+\sigma_C,
\qquad |\mathcal D_K|\ge q-k+\sigma_C+r_B,
\]

where (r_B\ge\max\{2N_K-\sigma_C,w_B\}). The phase argument now includes
**every** degree-at-most-(K) physical exceptional face touching the outer
contact walk, through one pocket/face phase transfer. Under the same
conditional residual/tail hypotheses, the rank payment cancels (5m_B):

\[
4S+2\sigma_R\ge2(\pi+s)D+5(\sigma_C+r_B+S_U)
 +2(Q-f)+2(b-P_F)-o(D).
\]

Thus nonunit hull sides alone cannot pay this branch. It also forces
(\liminf f_{\rm in}/D\ge s), where these exceptional faces have **no outer
contact edge and no loaded vertex**. Large singletons/rhombic excess,
positive residual, and persistent pocket tails still survive. Classification:
finite proved candidate and conditional synthesis awaiting independent audit.

## Inspected branches and rejected shortcuts

[Global phase access](../docs/reports/target_c_global_phase_access_integrable_branch_exclusion_2026-10-05.md)
now excludes the full-core Type-II branch with `R_F=o(D)` and both uniformly
integrable exceptional-face degrees and outer-pocket lengths. Actual
internal train columns are independent, giving `e(S)<=2|S|-2` and
`|boundary S|>=Q_S+4`. This bounds average graph distance to the outer walk.
Groemer direction stability, fixed-radius small-set mass control, and hull
normal dispersion then force **all** trains to carry `o(D^2)` rhombi,
contradicting Type II. This is a conditional branch elimination awaiting
independent audit, not a Level I settlement.

The marked-face bank and the weighted synthesis are two forms of the same
exact count: `4S+2sigma_R=4T-8sqrt(R_4)`. After cancellation of `m_B`, its
bound is equivalent to `2f>=2sD+sigma_C+r_B+S_U-o(D)`. These inequalities
must not be spent as independent charges. Global phase access supplies a
new contradiction beyond this scalar restatement.

#663 tip `70e2f6a95adcc5bac1ade91da9ea26ffdfe78cfd`: all-unit end currency
agrees with #699's remaining-train identity; no new canonical promotion.
#668 tip `a2ccd6161519c7d27482a7c6e751cd44e595e1b6`: finite local contact routing
and persistent high-degree tail. #671 tip
`0e49b450cc4819cc2f4f205303cbb9a09b45d269`: pinned separator and face-local
loaded returns. Their cap applications remain conditional on strong open-cell
extraction. None of their conclusions is silently imported as canonical.

The finite #696 exact multishear chart, positive KKT left kernel, and mixed
rigidity imply local isolation of its origin when an unselected contact
remains. This qualitative obstruction was already preserved in open salvage
#675 (`1af5583ac559f0cc3e2e1ee1e7fbdcc6a8d6d99b`); it is not a new theorem of
this run. A strict competitor must leave that local exact-contact chart or
change its hypotheses. Quadratic energy alone cannot override the positive
spanning first-order obstruction.

## Exact surviving branches and closing threshold

The [actual loaded pentagon regression](../docs/reports/target_c_phase_frustration_fixed_wall_activation_regression_2026-10-05.md)
kills direct fixed-wall activation of the direction-frustration bank:
positive residual plus global optimality, positive actual KKT stress and
mixed rigidity need not give even one spare interior site. Deleting any one
loaded boundary point also leaves no inward vacancy. It is the genuine
finite optimum `D(5)=phi`, not a large-Type-II family. Summing positive
residuals across disjoint prescribed walls still gives no independent slot
currency. The new bank needs large-source coupling or a proved collective
movement of its walls.

[Augmented train phase rank](../docs/reports/target_c_augmented_train_phase_rank_small_residual_exclusion_2026-10-05.md)
supersedes the two-tail restriction above: **the entire full-core Type-II
`R_F=o(D)` branch is excluded**, at unreviewed proof-candidate scope.
Fixing auxiliary hull-side vector displacements makes all internal angular
train columns independent on physical faces **and pockets**. For any node
set, `e(U)<=2|U|-2`. In one phase bin, `N_j<=10|H|+4E_j`: large nodes are
charged by count, good small pockets by their distinct hull anchors. This
avoids all tail-mass assumptions and contradicts quadratic rhombus saturation.
Every pocket, including a four-sided one with a nonunit added chord,
has explicit closure rows. Only original strict unit rhombi propagate
opposite-side train rates automatically; the finite verifier checks this
classification separately.
The original six-point global minimizer (circumradius-one pentagon plus
center) also passes the actual-force augmented-column audit, including
the case of no unit hull side and five old contact bridges. It has no
rhombi and is not a large-diameter Type-II packet. Assigned boundary
isolates retain their unique chamber assignment in the frustration bank.

Without assuming small residual, fixed cutoffs and angular tolerances force
`liminf B_bad/D>=1/(240sqrt(3))` direction-frustrated bounded-degree
chambers. Eventually a boundary-vertex-disjoint family has size at least
`D/(2400sqrt(3)K)`, where `K` is the fixed boundary cutoff. Each chamber
pays a fixed positive Groemer residual. This matching requires activation
or a collective source replacement; no contact activation is presumed.
The parameter recipe is universal: `M=L=100000`,
`n=ceil(1000pi^2 L/Delta_2)`, `epsilon=pi/(3n)`,
`eta=Delta_2 epsilon/(3000pi^2)`. With
`kappa_fr=sigma_100000(eta)/(240sqrt(3))>0`, every full-core Type-II
sequence obeys `liminf R_F/D>=kappa_fr`. The exact population budget is
`delta_F+E_4+a0 R_F<c0 P_F+a0 Z_ext`; hence
`limsup (delta_F+E_4-a0 Z_ext)/D<=c0pi-a0 kappa_fr`.
There is no effective estimate for the compactness threshold or `D_0`.

[Terminal short-pocket depletion](../docs/reports/target_c_terminal_short_pocket_physical_frustration_2026-10-05.md)
removes an additional escape in the live scope `q/D->pi, u_B=o(D)`, with
no low-`t_D` restriction. Two-step pocket chords tend to unit length and
their contact phases track the actual hull. Longer-pocket terminal mass is
at most `3u_B`. All outer-ended trains therefore carry `o(D^2)` rhombi,
without a small-residual assumption. Retaining both outer-rank and good-hull
counts, the bank is `2f>=2sD+max(sigma_C,k-m_B)+S_U-o(D)` and cancels
the `5m_B` escape in (S). The maximum preserves the older stronger charge
when `m_B` is small; its two terms are not additive.

In this scope a universal positive normalized residual floor is required
on **physical unit-wall exceptional faces themselves**, even if a few long
pockets carry linear residual. A linear boundary-vertex-disjoint family
of physical direction-frustrated walls is forced. No slot capacity or
activation follows; the exact shield is available if a collective
replacement is proved. Terminal `u_B=Omega(D)` remains outside this result.

[Loaded flat-pentagon second depletion](../docs/reports/target_c_loaded_flat_pentagon_second_depletion_2026-10-05.md)
selects physical walls automatically in the live `x_B=o(D)` branch.
An almost straight loaded degree-two pentagon corner forces the complete
face phase to follow the hull, without a residual hypothesis. The marked
bank has size `g>=q-e_BI-6(Q-f)-o(D)` and rank exactly `2g`, witnessed by
two actual hull singleton columns per marked face. Depletion gives
`2(f-g)>=2sD+sigma_C+S_U-o(D)`, hence
`e_BI+6(Q-f)>=sD+2k+(sigma_C+S_U)/2-o(D)`.
This excludes an attachment/degree budget below that threshold. Marked
pentagon residual tends to zero; their hidden chords remain strict.
The trapezoid limit has prior art; the new converse and simultaneous
loaded-hull depletion use no superseded low-terminal hypotheses.

### Formal scalar survivor after composition

The following **leading coefficients**, not a source construction, satisfy
the hull, outer and marked-face banks simultaneously:

`q=pi, m_B=u_B=0, k=pi/8, Q=f=3pi/4, sigma_C=S_U=0`,
`e_BI=(pi+s)/2, g=(pi-s)/2, T=19pi/8`,
`|D_marked|=15pi/8-s, U=pi/2+s, R_phys=R_F=1/4`,
`delta_F=E_4=Z_ext=0` at linear order.

Here `g=q-e_BI`, `U>=2s`, and `f-g=pi/4+s/2>s`; both strict
inequalities follow from `s<pi/2`. The actual population inequality has
positive margin `pi/2-1/4`. Compactness thresholds may be normalized below
one, so the new nonexplicit floors are also respected. Taking `S=q`
gives `sigma_R=11pi/4-4s>=0`; the weighted ledgers retain their positive
surplus. Boundary-face counts can be `F_B=e_BI`,
`F_in=pi/4-s/2>0`. These assignments have no claimed unit-distance
embedding, stress, global optimality or isolate realization.

This exact scalar regression prevents falsely declaring closure by adding
overlapping payments. A geometric/source coupling must invalidate it;
the present scalar identities alone do not do so.

### Positive reciprocal internal endpoint graph

[The reciprocal train candidate](../docs/reports/target_c_positive_reciprocal_internal_train_graph_2026-10-05.md)
integrates the actual positive contact stress on every bounded augmented
face. For an internal train with terminal vector `w` at `f`,
`q_g-q_f=-A_tau Jw`, where `A_tau=sum_(e in tau) alpha_e>0`.
The angular matrix is the transpose of the actual reciprocal bar rigidity
matrix scaled by `1/A_tau`. Mixed rigidity then excludes every repeated
bounded endpoint pair, including different-direction pairs and pocket
endpoints. Every node subset satisfies componentwise `(2,3)` sparsity.

The third row dependency is reciprocal rotation `Jq`; the construction
uses no generic-rank claim. This removes same-pair reuse from a global
bounded-face return argument. The finite deficit does not alter the
leading coefficient `2f`, so the formal scalar survivor above remains
compatible. Force-space lengths `A_tau` are not source route currency.

[Terminal-wall-disjoint bulk](../docs/reports/target_c_pentagon_terminal_wall_disjoint_quadratic_bulk_2026-10-05.md)
globalizes the low-endpoint-defect pentagon-pair crossing family. Trains
whose own pentagon walls share a source vertex have at most four rhombi;
all other terminal-wall conflicts have degree at most 250. Exact
Bernoulli thinning retains `(c_250 Delta_2-o(1))D^2` actual crossings
with pairwise vertex-disjoint terminal walls, where
`c_250=(1/251)^2(250/251)^500>0`. After removing short selected trains,
a linear family has macroscopically separated actual contact-edge
midpoint endpoints and still carries quadratic crossings.

This applies when `m_B,u_B,Q-f=o(D)`; the pentagon-pair occurrence
argument was checked at automation branch commit `cae7122a`. No
reciprocal-rank premise is needed for thinning. The selected train
interiors cross, and pentagon endpoints are not necessarily loaded.
The result supplies separate source walls and genuine crossing currency,
but does not earn second depletion or a dual-tree feasible radius.

[Complete pentagon closure elimination](../docs/reports/target_c_all_pentagon_closure_core_elimination_2026-10-05.md)
now removes pentagon-only stalled closure cores of **every size**. In
any pentagon subset the internal endpoint graph has a node of degree at
most three, hence two nonparallel external pivot trains. Restriction of
the pure-contact dual closure kernel to higher-face blocks is injective:
`sigma_C<=2 f_6<=2(Q-f)`. Thus `Q-f=o(D)` forces `sigma_C=o(D)` without
phase, residual or terminal hypotheses; `Q-f=0` gives exact zero corank.

When all exceptional faces are pentagons, a complete two-anchor order
gives a finite local exact contact chart of dimension `q-k` (including
rotation). Isolates stay fixed and every original lower constraint is
retained locally. Active diameter feasibility, a uniform radius and a
finite escape from the diameter cage are still missing. This discharges
the earlier two-anchor integration alternative in its nonterminal
all-pentagon scope, without reviving the empty low-terminal windows.
Pure `sigma_C` is distinct from the pinned-component surplus `s_C` in
`mu_D`; (P.1) cannot be substituted for a pinned-surplus upper bound.

[Complete face elimination](../docs/reports/target_c_complete_face_elimination_and_contact_regularity_2026-10-05.md)
strengthens the pentagon result to **every** canonical triangle-free
C-II source in the mixed-rigidity regime: `sigma_C=0`,
`rank(C_face)=2f`, `rank(R_C)=e`. Positive unloaded equilibrium makes
physical face corners strict. In an induced endpoint graph some face
has internal degree at most three. A pentagon then has two nonparallel
external ends; any higher-degree face has at least three external ends,
which cannot all share one projective direction. Thus elimination reaches
all faces, including the persistent high-degree tail.

The full contact realization space is smooth, with core dimension
`q-k+2`; the complete train chart has dimension `q-k` after translation.
Every source point is retained. The chart radius can shrink with pivot
determinants and actual pair slacks, and no active-upper descent follows.
The exact finite identity on any bar realization is
`sum_H beta_h |p'_h|^2=D^2-sum_c delta_c^T Omega delta_c`.
Actual pentagon targets show that its strict weighted contraction can
either lengthen the maximum or collide vertices. Pure `sigma_C=0` does
not bound pinned `s_C` and does not invalidate the scalar survivor.

