## One-vacancy collective motion and strict capacity (2026-10-05)

[V.1](../docs/reports/target_c_one_vacancy_collective_strictification_2026-10-05.md)
strictifies every remaining interior point of a strict oblique rectangular
unit grid with one interior vacancy. Stage one moves the vacant row/column
in perpendicular directions; stage two expands the four stationary blocks
in the dual basis. Every wall point and every starting label is retained;
all intermediate lower constraints and strict containment are preserved.
The starting cardinality is N-1, not a hidden deletion from an N-point source.

Combined with fixed-wall uniqueness, ordinary interior capacity K and strict
interior capacity K-1 occur at arbitrarily large sizes. There are quadratic
contact-isolated populations behind linear unit walls with no strict spare
slot. These are container-capacity examples, not actual global diameter
minimizers or canonical contact-minimal sources. This kills an unqualified
quadratic-isolate/linear-wall strict-refill implication. Spending the positive
motion in canonical §162 still requires an actual source-compatible vacancy
and control of the external interface and upper diameter constraints.

## Actual unit-wall activation (2026-10-05)

[W.1--W.6](../docs/reports/target_c_vacancy_funded_unit_wall_activation_2026-10-05.md)
spend the vacancy motions through genuine contact minimality. A unit wall
edge crossing a new/exterior pair gives distance at least sqrt(3). A deleted
wall vertex can fund one extra interior point: old exterior points and new
points remain separated from its old coordinate, so that coordinate still
certifies shielding without being counted in the new source.

An exact strict-oblique m-by-n grid wall in a canonical C-II source must
enclose at least K=(m-1)(n-1) actual source points. V.1 supplies strict
capacity K-1; flat-wall positive equilibrium forces an interior contact,
so any smaller population contradicts contact minimality. In the finite
fixed-wall uniqueness window, the full interior must be the exact grid.

At the triangular limit, two adjacent vacancies have an explicit sequential
release order for m,n>=3, giving K-2 strict interior points. Its positive
endpoint margin survives sufficiently close actual simple unit cycles,
with a tolerance depending on the fixed frame. Such an actual cycle cannot
enclose K-3 or fewer source points; at K-2 all enclosed points must be
contact-isolated. All lower and upper constraints and source labels are
accounted for. No theorem here forces the complete cycle or its integer
deficiency from the general full-core/macroscopic-container ledger.

[B.3](../docs/reports/target_c_boundary_vacancy_funded_collective_refill_2026-10-05.md)
strengthens the robust threshold: a sufficiently close fixed triangular
rectangular unit cycle cannot enclose K-2 or fewer source points. Delete
two adjacent actual side-wall vertices and release all K reference interior
positions through that boundary opening. The deleted labels fund the two
extra slots. A relaxed crossing bound sqrt(4t^2-1), t>=19/20, shields each
original reference position; displacement below 1/100 leaves every new
point farther than 3/2 from every retained exterior source point. Final
points need not avoid deleted wall coordinates. This removes the previous
deficiency-two contact-isolated alternative for these fixed frames, while
leaving the general interface/population extraction obligation open.

[P.1](../docs/reports/target_c_two_side_polynomial_collective_refill_2026-10-05.md)
supplies an explicit growing-frame criterion. Opening the lower/left sides
of any unit oblique m-by-n frame with angle in [60,90] degrees removes
J=m+n-1 pins. A simultaneous bisector
motion strictifies all K=(m-1)(n-1) interior points with squared gap
3/[250000*(m+n)^14] and wall tolerance gap/[4*(m+n+1)]. If an actual wall
meets that tolerance and encloses at most K-J points, all deleted labels
are funded by the strict refill and contact minimality is contradicted.
For an actual convex inactive chamber this gives residual
r_W <= mn*(sin(phi)/a0-1)+(m+n)-2
 + [2(m+n)*eta+(m+n)*eta^2]/a0. The generic linear residual
ledger does not cross this threshold or furnish the required wall chart.

## One-pin oblique activation with no boundary residual loss (2026-10-05)

[O.1](../docs/reports/target_c_one_boundary_pin_oblique_refill_2026-10-05.md)
strictifies all K=(m-1)(n-1) reference interior points after deleting only
wall label (1,0), for every 60<phi<=90 degrees. A column release followed
by perpendicular expansion of the remaining block gives explicit gap
(1-2cos(phi))^4/[25000000000000*(m+n)^20]. The actual-unit-cycle tolerance
is gap/[4*(m+n+1)]. This is a source replacement, with all old source labels
accounted for, not an identification of old interior points with a grid.
Every contact-minimal triangle-free global source with that actual wall
has at least K enclosed points. For convex walls:

r_W <= mn*(sin(phi)/a0-1)+[2L*eta+L*eta^2]/a0, L=m+n.

The former linear boundary allowance L-2 is removed. A framed residual
bank exceeding its total angular-area and wall-error allowance is excluded.
Canonical RF>=kappa*D does not itself provide capture in such frames.
At phi=60 the one-pin reference has the exact gap rho=0 or
rho>=a0/[2*(m+n)]; it admits no nonconstant continuous feasible release.
This is a triangular pinned regression, not a diameter-optimal counterexample.

[Two-pin strict capacity](../docs/reports/target_c_triangular_two_pin_strict_capacity_2026-10-05.md)
is exactly K for every triangular 3-by-n frame and the triangular 4-by-4
square. An elementary unit-triangle cover, with a six-point unit-disk
obstruction in the square, proves the upper bounds for arbitrary targets.
Thus the K-site two-pin construction cannot universally be upgraded to
K+1. A theorem for both side lengths tending to infinity is still separate;
these pinned frames contain unit triangles and have no global-D certificate.

## Canonical-stress traffic compression (2026-10-05)

[Traffic domination](../docs/reports/target_c_multishear_traffic_domination_2026-10-05.md)
proves W=diag(A)-B=R^T*Omega*R>=0 for actual noncrossing outer-train cuts
and the canonical PSD stress. Its scalar kernel has dimension 2 minus the
span rank of unselected contact directions. With two such directions W is
positive definite. Every finite angle vector has weighted old-diameter sum
D^2-delta_x^T*W*delta_x-delta_y^T*W*delta_y. For one cut A>B eventually
in a full-core source, because indicator equality requires at most two
parallel lines and |V|<=2*floor(D)+2. This settles the finite mean-energy
sign for that stress. It does not give a common maximum contraction.
All one-cut lower and upper pair constraints are exact quadratics in
tan(theta/2), including old inactive upper pairs and isolates. The separate
local diameter-coordinate report imported from main remains unreviewed.

## Final finding and user-requested wrap (2026-10-05)

[Universal pentagon capacity](../docs/reports/target_c_unit_pentagon_perimeter_capacity_2026-10-05.md)
proves that any five unit-separated planar points have hull perimeter at
least five. Hence a strictly convex unit pentagon with separated wall
vertices has a unique five-point packing, its vertices. Retaining 5-d
vertices after d>=1 deletions permits at most d-1 interior replacements;
retaining all five permits none. For a source-vertex-disjoint bank of a
activated walls the total capacity is at most total deletions minus a.
This persists through contact-preserving motions that keep each final
wall simple and strictly convex. Individual pentagon interiors therefore
cannot replenish their deleted labels. A larger collective region or a
release of the unit-wall constraints is required for that mechanism.
The result is a proved candidate awaiting independent audit and changes
no canonical status. Both full-core C-II and the macroscopic-container
branch remain open. The user explicitly requested wrap-up; no Level I
settlement is claimed.
